 "id": "2026-10-24-champi-okinawa-record-rain",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Okinawa just got record rain from Typhoon Champi. Is Japan's mainland next?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Iriomote Island in Okinawa recorded five hundred sixty-seven millimeters of rain in forty-eight hours. Jiji Press says that is a new record for that location. Japan's weather agency issued a level four landslide warning for parts of the prefecture."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Saturday afternoon, Champi was about two hundred fifty kilometers north of Yonaguni Island, moving north-northeast. Central pressure was nine hundred eighty-five hectopascals. The agency says it could approach Kyushu on Monday, then become an extratropical cyclone, and urges caution about heavy rain."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Reuters reports Japan Airlines, ANA and Skymark canceled more than one hundred flights from Thursday to Sunday, affecting over eleven thousand passengers. Organizers also canceled the Okinawa Industrial Festival, which expected hundreds of thousands of visitors."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will Champi bring heavy rain to Kyushu on Monday? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
